  "open_items": [
    {
      "id": "pair_builder",
      "kind": "missing_evidence",
      "detail": "The code that sampled the 42 admissions and built the blinded/keyed pair files (2026-09-16 15:04 UTC) was not found. The pre-rating protocol names a seeded sampling script for its own, different frame (60 dev admissions per stage); that script was not found either (local projects, knowledge base, default branches of the DATEXIS pipeline repositories), and the executed batch does not follow its frame."
    },
    {
      "id": "zero_shot_generation",
      "kind": "missing_evidence",
      "detail": "The pre-rating protocol defines the zero-shot condition as the same generator (Qwen3-32B) and prompts without the loop, taken from a base evaluation run (4 candidates, first valid JSON). The outputs of that run were not found; none of the 84 zero-shot texts occurs in the stored loop-construction outputs of any model. The served texts, word counts and a recorded zero-shot verifier score exist."
    },
    {
      "id": "protocol_deviation",
      "kind": "missing_evidence",
      "detail": "A pre-rating protocol (internal, self-dated 2026-09-16, no independent timestamp) specified a different study - 60 dev admissions per stage sampled 30 per loop outcome, three 1-5 items (evidence support, conclusion support, clinical soundness), a third rater on a 40-trace overlap, and a paired analysis of the mean item score. The executed audit used 42 held-out test admissions, binary Q1/Q2 plus two preferences, two raters on everything and a binary composite with an admission-cluster bootstrap. The deviations are not documented in a dated amendment."
    },
    {
      "id": "mimic_version",
      "kind": "missing_evidence",
      "detail": "MIMIC-IV release version is not recorded in the audit artifacts (repository mentions both 2.2 and 3.1)."
    },
    {
      "id": "checkpoint_volume_not_inspected",
      "kind": "missing_evidence",
      "detail": "A large experiment-checkpoint volume on the cluster is not mounted by any running workload and was not inspected (read-only discovery); it may hold zero-shot generation outputs."
    },
    {
      "id": "claim:generator",
      "kind": "unverified_claim",
      "detail": "Appendix B: zero_shot_rationales_traced_to_generator_outputs: expected 84, observed 0"
    },
    {
      "id": "claim:dev_split",
      "kind": "manuscript_discrepancy",
      "detail": "Appendix B: source_split_values: expected ['dev'], observed ['test']"
    },
    {
      "id": "claim:criteria_and_preregistration",
      "kind": "manual_review",
      "detail": "The three named criteria are the 1-5 items of the pre-rating protocol, which were not used. Clinicians answered two per-rationale questions (Q1 evidence grounding, Q2 support for the target; Yes/No/Unclear) plus two pairwise preferences; there was no clinical-soundness rating. The rating interface and questions predate the first rating, but sample, instrument and analysis deviate from the pre-rating protocol, the executed analysis was implemented after all ratings, and a single-clinician unblinded preliminary analysis was written before the other clinician's last two saves."
    }
  ],
